  "articleBody": "Ever notice how your door swings freely in the summer but then suddenly starts sticking or dragging when winter rolls around? You're not alone! This is a super common question we get, and it often comes down to changes in humidity and temperature that cause wood to expand and contract. But sometimes, it's not just the door itself. Fluctuating groundwater levels or even subtle foundation movements can also impact how your door fits its frame throughout the year. It's easy to just blame the weather, but ignoring persistent seasonal sticking can lead to bigger issues. We always recommend checking if your door and frame are truly plumb and level. If they're not, or if you've done some flooring or foundation work recently, those changes can definitely throw things off. Trying to force it or just shaving off a bit of wood without understanding the root cause is a common mistake. If your door's behavior changes dramatically with the seasons, and simple adjustments aren't cutting it, that's often a signal that a professional look might be needed to really stabilize things and make sure it's not a symptom of something more substantial. We can help you get to the bottom of it!",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
